Also, the `showPush`/`openPush` functions are declared after use — function declarations are hoisted, fine.

Also `badge: absoluteUrl("/app-icon-192.png")` — the badge should be a monochrome icon; using the app icon is not ideal but acceptable. Actually, `badge` with a full-color PNG may render oddly on Android (it's masked to monochrome). Chrome will use the alpha channel. Let me just drop `badge` to avoid weirdness... Many apps set badge to a monochrome icon. Since we don't have one, I'll drop it.

Hmm, one more: TurboOffline's `start()` may add a `fetch` listener. Not an issue.

Also note: TurboOffline intercepts requests for documents; the notification URL navigation goes through the SW fetch handler — fine.

